      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the Burlington and Missouri River Railroad arrived in September 1859, it ran parallel to the Des Moines River through Ottumwa.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottumwa%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Jefferson Street Viaduct, spanning the Des Moines River, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
